.TH BLKSTREAM 1 "2026-11-24" "diffstream-tools 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
blkstream \- raw block device to DIFFSTR1 sparse/discard stream tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blkstream
.B \-\-source
.IR dev_or_file
.RB [ \-\-truncate
.IR size ]
.RB [ \-\-nocache ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B blkstream
reads a raw block device or disk image sequentially, detects zero-filled regions at 64 KiB granularity, and emits a wire-compatible
.B DIFFSTR1
stream (OP_TRUNCATE, OP_DATA, coalesced OP_HOLE, OP_EOF) for P2V migration or sparse replication.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-source " dev_or_file"
Source block device (e.g., /dev/sda, /dev/md0) or image file. Also accepts \fB\-\-change\fR as a CLI alias.
.TP
.B \-\-nocache
Advise sequential reads and drop pages via posix_fadvise(2).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print throughput, bytes written, and bytes discarded to stderr.
.TP
.BI \-\-truncate " size"
Clamp source stream size to \fIsize\fR (supports K/M/G/T suffixes) for V2P migration onto smaller disks.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B P2V migration from physical RAID array to sparse VM image:
blkstream --source /dev/md0 --nocache -v | zstd -T0 | ssh vm-host "zstd -d | diffstream --apply --target /var/lib/libvirt/images/vm.img --nocache"
.TP
.B Clamp a 100G disk stream onto an 80G target block device:
blkstream --source /dev/sda --truncate 80G --nocache -v | diffstream --apply --target /dev/nvme0n1 --noresize --taildiscard --nocache
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diffstream (1),
.BR thindiffstream (1),
.BR zfsdiffstream (1)
